<title>ITALY: FAO puts global wheat output at 581 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>FAO puts global wheat output at 581 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.N. Food and Agriculture Organisation (FAO) said on Monday it had raised its 1996 global wheat output forecast to 581 million tonnes.</p>
<p>The figure was 10 million tonnes higher than FAO's previous forecast issued in September and represented a 6.4 percent increase on the latest estimate for 1995 production.</p>
<p>&quot;The revision since the last report reflects mainly an increase in the estimate of production in the EU, where the harvest is now virtually complete and bumper crops are reported,&quot; the Rome-based agency said in a food outlook.</p>
<p>--Rome newsroom +39 6 678 2501</p>
